  <title xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Serbia - Support to Assisted Voluntary Return and Reintegration from the Western Balkans</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The objective of the development cooperation among the parties is twofold:

1.	To develop an online return counselling toolkit that shall be tested in the Western Balkans with key countries of origin that are a priority for the Western Balkans. The tool kit will respond to the return dynamics in the Western Balkans both as a sending and receiving region but will also be applicable for use globally. 

2.	To support the safe and dignified return and sustainable reintegration of migrants from the Western Balkans to their countries of origin, by complementing the current IOM AVRR programme in the Western Balkans. The proposed project is designed to respond to both short and longer-term challenges, working to further the institutionalization of a comprehensive, rights-based and sustainable regional AVRR program adapted to national contexts and in line with IOM&apos; Framework For Assisted Voluntary Return And Reintegration, IOM&#x2019;s Integrated Approach to Reintegration as well as the Reintegration Handbook implemented in full alignment with international standards, including the EU Return Acquis as well as principles of the Global Compact for Safe, Orderly and Regular Migration (GCM).</narrative>
  </description>
